msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Pásma SLSTR VIS/SWIR (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) zaznamenáva "
"žiarivosť na hornej hranici atmosféry v šiestich kanáloch odrazeného "
"slnečného žiarenia s rozlíšením 500 m: S1 (0,555 µm, vegetácia/aerosól), S2 "
"(0,659 µm, NDVI/aerosól), S3 (0,865 µm, NDVI/označovanie oblačnosti), S4 "
"(1,375 µm, detekcia cirrov), S5 (1,61 µm, ľad/sneh/vegetácia) a S6 (2,25 "
"µm, stav vegetácie). Každé pásmo je dostupné v nadirovom a šikmom pohľade, "
"čo umožňuje dvojuhlové pozorovanie zemského a oceánskeho povrchu. Produkt "
"L1B obsahuje geolokované, kalibrované žiarivosti vytvorené kalibráciou "
"signálu, prevzorkovaním do siete a označovaním oblačnosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# Termálne infračervené pásma SLSTR (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) zaznamenáva "
"jasové teploty na hornej hranici atmosféry v troch termálnych "
"infračervených kanáloch s rozlíšením 1 km: S7 (3,74 µm, teplota povrchu "
"mora/zeme a detekcia požiarov), S8 (10,85 µm, teplota povrchu mora/zeme a "
"detekcia požiarov) a S9 (12,0 µm, teplota povrchu mora/zeme). Každé pásmo "
"je dostupné v nadirovom a šikmom pohľade, čo umožňuje dvojuhlové "
"pozorovanie pre lepšiu atmosférickú korekciu a určovanie teploty povrchu. "
"Produkt L1B obsahuje geolokované, kalibrované jasové teploty vytvorené "
"kalibráciou signálu, prevzorkovaním do siete a označovaním oblačnosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Termálne infračervené pásma emisií požiarov\n"
"\n"
"Prístroj Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) má "
"dva vyhradené kanály (F1 a F2), ktoré slúžia na detekciu teploty zemského "
"povrchu (LST). Kanál F2 so stredovou vlnovou dĺžkou 10854 nm meria v "
"termálnej infračervenej oblasti (TIR). Je veľmi užitočný na monitorovanie "
"požiarov a udalostí s vysokou teplotou s rozlíšením 1 km.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Výška základne oblakov\n"
"\n"
"Výška základne oblakov meraná v metroch (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Tlak na základni oblakov\n"
"\n"
"Tlak meraný na základni oblakov v pascaloch (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Effective radiometric cloud fraction\n"
"\n"
"Effective radiometric cloud fraction represents the portion of the Earth's "
"surface covered by clouds, divided by the total surface. Clouds have "
"shielding, albedo, and in-cloud absorption effects on trace gas retrieval. "
"The effective radiometric cloud fraction is an important parameter to "
"correct these effects."
msgstr ""
"# Efektívny radiometrický podiel oblačnosti\n"
"\n"
"Efektívny radiometrický podiel oblačnosti vyjadruje časť zemského povrchu "
"pokrytú oblakmi vo vzťahu k celkovému povrchu. Oblaky majú pri určovaní "
"stopových plynov tieniaci efekt, efekt albeda a absorpcie v oblaku. "
"Efektívny radiometrický podiel oblačnosti je dôležitý parameter na korekciu "
"týchto efektov."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Optická hrúbka oblakov\n"
"\n"
"Hrúbka oblakov je kľúčový parameter na charakterizáciu optických vlastností "
"oblakov. Je mierou toho, koľko slnečného svetla prejde oblakom a dostane sa "
"na zemský povrch. Čím vyššia je optická hrúbka oblaku, tým viac slnečného "
"svetla oblak rozptyľuje a odráža. Tmavomodrá farba ukazuje miesta s nízkymi "
"hodnotami optickej hrúbky oblakov a červená väčšiu optickú hrúbku oblakov."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Výška vrcholu oblakov\n"
"\n"
"Výška vrcholu oblakov meraná v metroch (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Tlak na vrchole oblakov\n"
"\n"
"Tlak meraný na vrchole oblakov v pascaloch (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Termálne pásmo 10\n"
"\n"
"Táto termálna vizualizácia je založená na pásme 10 (pásmo je oblasť "
"elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych "
"pásmach). Pri stredovej vlnovej dĺžke 10895 nm meria v termálnej "
"infračervenej oblasti (TIR). Namiesto merania teploty vzduchu, ako to robia "
"meteorologické stanice, pásmo 10 zaznamenáva samotný povrch zeme, ktorý je "
"často omnoho teplejší. Termálne pásmo 10 je užitočné na zisťovanie teplôt "
"povrchu a zbiera sa s rozlíšením 100 metrov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1).\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index je jednoduchý, ale účinný index na "
"kvantifikáciu zelenej vegetácie. Je mierou zdravia vegetácie na základe "
"toho, ako rastliny odrážajú svetlo pri určitých vlnových dĺžkach. Rozsah "
"hodnôt NDVI je od -1 do 1. Záporné hodnoty NDVI (hodnoty blížiace sa k -1) "
"zodpovedajú vode. Hodnoty blízke nule (-0,1 až 0,1) vo všeobecnosti "
"zodpovedajú holým plochám skál, piesku alebo snehu. Nízke kladné hodnoty "
"predstavujú krovinatú vegetáciu a trávne porasty (približne 0,2 až 0,4), "
"kým vysoké hodnoty označujú lesy mierneho pásma a tropické dažďové pralesy "
"(hodnoty blížiace sa k 1).\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index as "
"it corrects for soil background signals and atmospheric influences. It is "
"very useful in areas of dense canopy cover. The range of values for EVI is "
"-1 to 1, with healthy vegetation generally around 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More infos [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) "
"and [here.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"
msgstr ""
"# Vylepšený vegetačný index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"Vylepšený vegetačný index (EVI) je „optimalizovaný“ vegetačný index, "
"pretože koriguje signály pozadia pôdy a atmosférické vplyvy. Je veľmi "
"užitočný v oblastiach s hustým zápojom korún. Rozsah hodnôt EVI je od -1 do "
"1, pričom zdravá vegetácia sa vo všeobecnosti pohybuje okolo 0,20 až 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) a "
"[tu.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosféricky odolný vegetačný index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Atmosféricky odolný vegetačný index (ARVI) je vegetačný index, ktorý "
"minimalizuje účinky atmosférického rozptylu. Je najužitočnejší v oblastiach "
"s vysokým obsahom atmosférického aerosólu (hmla, prach, dym, znečistenie "
"ovzdušia). Rozsah ARVI je od -1 do 1, pričom zelená vegetácia sa vo "
"všeobecnosti pohybuje v hodnotách od 0,20 do 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) a "
"[tu.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Pôdou upravený vegetačný index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Pôdou upravený vegetačný index je podobný normalizovanému diferenčnému "
"vegetačnému indexu (NDVI), ale používa sa v oblastiach s nízkym vegetačným "
"krytom (< 40 %). Index je transformačná technika, ktorá minimalizuje vplyv "
"jasu pôdy zo spektrálnych vegetačných indexov využívajúcich červené a "
"blízke infračervené (NIR) vlnové dĺžky. Index je užitočný pri analýze "
"mladých plodín, suchých oblastí s riedkou vegetáciou a odkrytých povrchov "
"pôdy.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) a "
"[tu.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Modifikovaný antokyánový reflektančný index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Antokyány sú pigmenty bežné vo vyšších rastlinách, ktoré spôsobujú ich "
"červené, modré a fialové sfarbenie. Poskytujú cenné informácie o "
"fyziologickom stave rastlín, pretože sa považujú za ukazovatele rôznych "
"typov stresu rastlín. Odrazivosť antokyánov je najvyššia okolo 550 nm. "
"Rovnaké vlnové dĺžky však odráža aj chlorofyl. Na izolovanie antokyánov sa "
"odpočíta spektrálne pásmo 700 nm, ktoré odráža iba chlorofyl a nie "
"antokyány.\n"
"\n"
"Na korekciu hustoty a hrúbky listov sa k základnému indexu ARI pripočíta "
"blízke infračervené spektrálne pásmo (v odporúčaných vlnových dĺžkach "
"760-800 nm), ktoré súvisí s rozptylom na listoch. Nový index sa nazýva "
"modifikovaný ARI alebo mARI (aj ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"Hodnoty mARI pre skúmané stromy v [tomto pôvodnom "
"článku](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) sa "
"pohybovali od 0 do 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Skript Zelené mesto\n"
"\n"
"Skript Zelené mesto sa snaží zvýšiť povedomie o zelených plochách v mestách "
"po celom svete. Skript zohľadňuje normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index "
"(NDVI) a vlnové dĺžky skutočných farieb; oddeľuje zastavané oblasti od "
"zarastených, vďaka čomu je užitočný na detekciu mestských oblastí. "
"Zastavané oblasti sú zobrazené sivou a vegetácia zelenou farbou.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Skript Klasifikácia mestských oblastí\n"
"\n"
"Skript Klasifikácia mestských oblastí sa snaží detegovať zastavané oblasti "
"ich oddelením od holej pôdy, vegetácie a vody. Oblasti s vysokým obsahom "
"vlhkosti sú vrátené modrou farbou; oblasti označujúce zastavané plochy sú "
"vrátené bielou; zarastené oblasti zelenou; všetko ostatné označuje holú "
"pôdu a je zobrazené hnedými farbami.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Skript Mestská krajina v infračervených farbách\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript, ktorý vytvoril Leo Tolari, kombinuje vizualizáciu skutočných "
"farieb s blízkymi infračervenými (NIR) a krátkovlnnými infračervenými "
"(SWIR) vlnovými dĺžkami. Skript zvýrazňuje mestské oblasti lepšie ako "
"skutočné farby, pričom stále vyzerá prirodzene.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# NDMI pre stres z nedostatku vlhkosti\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný index vlhkosti (NDMI) pre stres z nedostatku "
"vlhkosti sa dá použiť na detekciu zavlažovania. Pri všetkých hodnotách "
"indexu nad 0 je pri znalosti využitia a pokrytia územia možné určiť, či "
"došlo k zavlažovaniu. Ak poznáme typ pestovanej plodiny (napr. citrusy), je "
"možné zistiť, či je zavlažovanie počas kľúčovej letnej vegetačnej sezóny "
"účinné, ako aj zistiť, či sú niektoré časti farmy nedostatočne alebo "
"nadmerne zavlažované.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný index vlhkosti (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný index vlhkosti (NDMI) sa používa na určenie obsahu "
"vody vo vegetácii a monitorovanie sucha. Rozsah hodnôt NDMI je od -1 do 1. "
"Záporné hodnoty NDMI (hodnoty blížiace sa k -1) zodpovedajú holej pôde. "
"Hodnoty okolo nuly (-0,2 až 0,4) vo všeobecnosti zodpovedajú vodnému "
"stresu. Vysoké kladné hodnoty predstavujú hustý porast bez vodného stresu "
"(približne 0,4 až 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný vodný index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný vodný index je najvhodnejší na mapovanie vodných "
"plôch. Hodnoty vodných plôch sú vyššie ako 0,5. Vegetácia má nižšie "
"hodnoty. Zastavané prvky majú kladné hodnoty medzi nulou a 0,2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) and [here.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v nepravých farbách\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit v nepravých farbách používa na snímkovanie Zeme aspoň jednu "
"neviditeľnú vlnovú dĺžku. Veľmi populárny je kompozit v nepravých farbách "
"využívajúci pásma blízkeho infračerveného, červeného a zeleného svetla "
"(pásmo je oblasť elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať "
"Zem v rôznych pásmach). Kompozit v nepravých farbách sa najčastejšie "
"používa na posúdenie hustoty a zdravia rastlín, pretože rastliny odrážajú "
"blízke infračervené a zelené svetlo, zatiaľ čo červené pohlcujú. Mestá a "
"odkrytá pôda sú sivé alebo žltohnedé a voda vyzerá modro alebo čierno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) a [tu.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v nepravých farbách\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit v nepravých farbách používa na snímkovanie Zeme aspoň jednu "
"neviditeľnú vlnovú dĺžku. Veľmi populárny je kompozit v nepravých farbách "
"využívajúci pásma blízkeho infračerveného, červeného a zeleného svetla "
"(pásmo je oblasť elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať "
"Zem v rôznych pásmach). Kompozit v nepravých farbách sa najčastejšie "
"používa na posúdenie hustoty a zdravia rastlín, pretože rastliny odrážajú "
"blízke infračervené a zelené svetlo, zatiaľ čo červené pohlcujú. Mestá a "
"odkrytá pôda sú sivé alebo žltohnedé a voda vyzerá modro alebo čierno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."

msgid ""
"# True color optimized\n"
"\n"
"This optimized True color script uses the visible light bands red, green "
"and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting "
"in a product with natural colours that represents the Earth as humans would "
"naturally see it. The visualisation uses highlight compression and improves "
"the contrast and color vividness through minor contrast and saturation "
"enhancement.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info for "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) "
"and for "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."
msgstr ""
"# Optimalizované skutočné farby\n"
"\n"
"Tento optimalizovaný skript skutočných farieb používa pásma viditeľného "
"svetla červené, zelené a modré v zodpovedajúcich červených, zelených a "
"modrých farebných kanáloch, výsledkom čoho je produkt s prirodzenými "
"farbami, ktorý zobrazuje Zem tak, ako by ju prirodzene videl človek. "
"Vizualizácia využíva kompresiu svetlých tónov a zlepšuje kontrast a živosť "
"farieb miernym zvýšením kontrastu a sýtosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií pre "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) a "
"pre "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum. Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. Landsat 8-9 has 11 bands. True color composite uses visible light "
"bands red, green and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color "
"channels, resulting in a natural colored product, that is a good "
"representation of the Earth as humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v skutočných farbách\n"
"\n"
"Senzory na satelitoch môžu snímať Zem v rôznych oblastiach "
"elektromagnetického spektra. Každá oblasť spektra sa nazýva pásmo. Landsat "
"8-9 má 11 pásiem. Kompozit v skutočných farbách používa pásma viditeľného "
"svetla červené, zelené a modré v zodpovedajúcich červených, zelených a "
"modrých farebných kanáloch, výsledkom čoho je produkt v prirodzených "
"farbách, ktorý dobre zobrazuje Zem tak, ako by ju prirodzene videl človek.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum . Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. True color composite uses visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v skutočných farbách\n"
"\n"
"Senzory na satelitoch môžu snímať Zem v rôznych oblastiach "
"elektromagnetického spektra. Každá oblasť spektra sa nazýva pásmo. Kompozit "
"v skutočných farbách používa pásma viditeľného svetla červené, zelené a "
"modré v zodpovedajúcich červených, zelených a modrých farebných kanáloch, "
"výsledkom čoho je produkt v prirodzených farbách, ktorý dobre zobrazuje Zem "
"tak, ako by ju prirodzene videl človek.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"

msgid ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"The colours of natural waters differ markedly across the globe, depending "
"on water composition and illumination conditions. Ocean colour instruments "
"measure water-leaving radiance in narrow spectral bands to retrieve "
"water-quality indicators. The true colour of natural waters is derived by "
"calculating tristimulus values — the three primaries (X, Y, Z) that specify "
"a colour stimulus as perceived by the human eye.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."
msgstr ""
"# Trichromatické hodnoty (Tristimulus)\n"
"\n"
"Farby prírodných vôd sa po celom svete výrazne líšia v závislosti od "
"zloženia vody a podmienok osvetlenia. Prístroje na meranie farby oceánu "
"merajú žiarivosť vystupujúcu z vody v úzkych spektrálnych pásmach s cieľom "
"získať ukazovatele kvality vody. Skutočná farba prírodných vôd sa odvodzuje "
"výpočtom trichromatických hodnôt — troch primárnych zložiek (X, Y, Z), "
"ktoré určujú farebný podnet vnímaný ľudským okom.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B05 (510 nm, cyan-green), and B02 (412.5 nm, violet) into "
"the red, green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a "
"near-infrared band used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it "
"in the red channel makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red "
"while water remains dark. B05 is sensitive to chlorophyll, sediment, "
"turbidity, and red tide, and B02 captures yellow dissolved organic matter "
"(CDOM) and detrital pigments. The composite is useful for ocean colour "
"analysis, coastal water quality monitoring, and distinguishing turbid or "
"sediment-laden waters from clear ocean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit v nepravých farbách zobrazuje pásma Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 "
"nm, blízke infračervené), B05 (510 nm, azúrovo-zelená) a B02 (412,5 nm, "
"fialová) v červenom, zelenom a modrom zobrazovacom kanáli. B17 je pásmo "
"blízkeho infračerveného svetla používané na korekciu aerosólov a atmosféry; "
"jeho umiestnením do červeného kanála sa vegetácia a povrch zeme javia jasne "
"červené, zatiaľ čo voda zostáva tmavá. B05 je citlivé na chlorofyl, "
"sedimenty, zákal a červený príliv a B02 zachytáva žltú rozpustenú organickú "
"látku (CDOM) a detritové pigmenty. Kompozit je užitočný na analýzu farby "
"oceánu, monitorovanie kvality pobrežných vôd a rozlišovanie zakalených "
"alebo sedimentmi zaťažených vôd od čistého oceánu.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B06 (560 nm, green), and B03 (442.5 nm, blue) into the red, "
"green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a near-infrared band "
"used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it in the red channel "
"makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red while water remains "
"dark. B06 is the chlorophyll absorption minimum reference band, and B03 "
"captures chlorophyll absorption and biogeochemical properties. Compared to "
"the B17/B05/B02 composite, the shifted green and blue channels offer a "
"different sensitivity to phytoplankton and dissolved organic matter in "
"coastal and open ocean waters.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit v nepravých farbách zobrazuje pásma Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 "
"nm, blízke infračervené), B06 (560 nm, zelená) a B03 (442,5 nm, modrá) v "
"červenom, zelenom a modrom zobrazovacom kanáli. B17 je pásmo blízkeho "
"infračerveného svetla používané na korekciu aerosólov a atmosféry; jeho "
"umiestnením do červeného kanála sa vegetácia a povrch zeme javia jasne "
"červené, zatiaľ čo voda zostáva tmavá. B06 je referenčné pásmo minima "
"absorpcie chlorofylu a B03 zachytáva absorpciu chlorofylu a biogeochemické "
"vlastnosti. V porovnaní s kompozitom B17/B05/B02 posunuté zelené a modré "
"kanály ponúkajú inú citlivosť na fytoplanktón a rozpustenú organickú látku "
"v pobrežných a otvorených oceánskych vodách.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to "
"even out the exposure. It makes clouds look natural and keep as much visual "
"information as possible. Sentinel-3 OLCI tiles cover large areas, making it "
"possible to observe large cloud formations, such as hurricanes.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"
msgstr ""
"# Vylepšená vizualizácia v skutočných farbách\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript využíva optimalizáciu svetlých tónov, aby sa predišlo "
"prepáleným pixelom a vyrovnala expozícia. Vďaka tomu vyzerajú oblaky "
"prirodzene a zachováva sa čo najviac vizuálnych informácií. Dlaždice "
"Sentinel-3 OLCI pokrývajú rozsiahle oblasti, čo umožňuje pozorovať veľké "
"oblačné útvary, napríklad hurikány.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"

msgid ""
"# Pansharpened True Color\n"
"\n"
"The pansharpened true color composite is done by using the usual true color "
"data (red, green and blue (RGB)) and enhancing them by using the "
"panchromatic band 8, or pan band (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). An image "
"from the pan band is similar to black-and-white film: it combines light "
"from the red, green, and blue parts of the spectrum into a single measure "
"of overall visible reflectance. Pansharpened images have 4x the resolution "
"of the usual true color composite, greatly enhancing the usefulness of "
"Landsat imagery.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."
msgstr ""
"# Skutočné farby so zostrením (pansharpening)\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit v skutočných farbách s pansharpeningom sa vytvára použitím "
"obvyklých údajov skutočných farieb (červená, zelená a modrá (RGB)) a ich "
"vylepšením pomocou panchromatického pásma 8, čiže pan pásma (pásmo je "
"oblasť elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v "
"rôznych pásmach). Snímka z pan pásma je podobná čiernobielemu filmu: "
"kombinuje svetlo z červenej, zelenej a modrej časti spektra do jedinej "
"miery celkovej odrazivosti vo viditeľnom svetle. Snímky s pansharpeningom "
"majú 4-krát vyššie rozlíšenie ako obvyklý kompozit v skutočných farbách, čo "
"výrazne zvyšuje užitočnosť snímok Landsat.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-landsat-"
"live-e4717cd7c356)."

msgid ""
"# False Color Urban composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite is used to visualise urbanized areas more clearly. "
"Vegetation is visible in shades of green, while urbanized areas are "
"represented by white, grey, or purple. Soils, sand, and minerals are shown "
"in a variety of colors. Snow and ice appear as dark blue, and water as "
"black or blue. Flooded areas are very dark blue and almost black. The "
"composite is useful for detecting wildfires and calderas of volcanoes, as "
"they are displayed in shades of red and yellow.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) and [here.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v nepravých farbách pre mestské oblasti\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit sa používa na jasnejšiu vizualizáciu urbanizovaných oblastí. "
"Vegetácia je viditeľná v odtieňoch zelenej, zatiaľ čo urbanizované oblasti "
"sú znázornené bielou, sivou alebo fialovou farbou. Pôdy, piesok a minerály "
"sú zobrazené v rôznych farbách. Sneh a ľad sa javia ako tmavomodré a voda "
"ako čierna alebo modrá. Zaplavené oblasti sú veľmi tmavomodré a takmer "
"čierne. Kompozit je užitočný na detekciu lesných požiarov a kalder sopiek, "
"pretože sú zobrazené v odtieňoch červenej a žltej.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) a [tu.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Agriculture composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared, near-infrared and blue bands to "
"monitor crop health (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Both short-wave and "
"near infrared bands are particularly good at highlighting dense vegetation, "
"which appears dark green in the composite. Crops appear in a vibrant green "
"and bare earth appears magenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) and "
"[here.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"
msgstr ""
"# Poľnohospodársky kompozit\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit využíva krátkovlnné infračervené, blízke infračervené a "
"modré pásma na monitorovanie zdravia plodín (pásmo je oblasť "
"elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych "
"pásmach). Krátkovlnné aj blízke infračervené pásma sú obzvlášť vhodné na "
"zvýraznenie hustej vegetácie, ktorá sa v kompozite javí tmavozelená. "
"Plodiny sa javia sýtozelené a holá pôda purpurová.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií [tu](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) a "
"[tu.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"

msgid ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"The Snow Classifier algorithm aims to detect snow by classifying pixels "
"based on different brightness and Normalized Difference Snow Index (NDSI) "
"thresholds. Values classified as snow are returned in bright vivid blue. "
"The script can overestimate snow areas over clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"
msgstr ""
"# Klasifikátor snehu\n"
"\n"
"Algoritmus Klasifikátor snehu sa snaží detegovať sneh klasifikáciou pixelov "
"na základe rôznych prahových hodnôt jasu a normalizovaného diferenčného "
"snehového indexu (NDSI). Hodnoty klasifikované ako sneh sú vrátené jasnou "
"sýtomodrou farbou. Skript môže nadhodnocovať snehové plochy v miestach s "
"oblačnosťou.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"

msgid ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"The script aims to dynamically visualise the chlorophyll and sediment "
"conditions of water bodies, which are primary indicators of water quality. "
"The chlorophyll content ranges in colors from dark blue (low chlorophyll "
"content) through green to red (high chlorophyll content). Sediment "
"concentrations are colored brown; opaque brown indicates high sediment "
"content.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"
msgstr ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"Skript sa snaží dynamicky vizualizovať stav chlorofylu a sedimentov vo "
"vodných plochách, ktoré sú primárnymi ukazovateľmi kvality vody. Obsah "
"chlorofylu sa pohybuje vo farbách od tmavomodrej (nízky obsah chlorofylu) "
"cez zelenú po červenú (vysoký obsah chlorofylu). Koncentrácie sedimentov sú "
"sfarbené hnedou; nepriehľadná hnedá označuje vysoký obsah sedimentov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"

msgid ""
"# Short wave infrared composite (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Short wave infrared (SWIR) measurements can help scientists estimate how "
"much water is present in plants and soil, as water absorbs SWIR "
"wavelengths. Short wave infrared bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) are also useful for distinguishing between cloud types (water clouds "
"versus ice clouds), snow and ice, all of which appear white in visible "
"light. In this composite vegetation appears in shades of green, soils and "
"built-up areas are in various shades of brown, and water appears black. "
"Newly burned land reflects strongly in SWIR bands, making them valuable for "
"mapping fire damages. Each rock type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v krátkovlnnom infračervenom svetle (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Merania v krátkovlnnom infračervenom svetle (SWIR) môžu vedcom pomôcť "
"odhadnúť, koľko vody sa nachádza v rastlinách a pôde, keďže voda pohlcuje "
"vlnové dĺžky SWIR. Krátkovlnné infračervené pásma (pásmo je oblasť "
"elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych "
"pásmach) sú tiež užitočné na rozlišovanie typov oblakov (vodné oblaky "
"verzus ľadové oblaky), snehu a ľadu, ktoré sa všetky vo viditeľnom svetle "
"javia biele. V tomto kompozite sa vegetácia javí v odtieňoch zelenej, pôdy "
"a zastavané oblasti v rôznych odtieňoch hnedej a voda sa javí čierna. "
"Čerstvo vyhorená krajina silno odráža v pásmach SWIR, vďaka čomu sú cenné "
"pri mapovaní škôd po požiaroch. Každý typ horniny odráža krátkovlnné "
"infračervené svetlo inak, čo umožňuje mapovať geológiu porovnávaním "
"odrazeného svetla SWIR.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný snehový index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný snehový index Sentinel-2 sa dá použiť na "
"rozlíšenie oblačnosti od snehovej pokrývky, pretože sneh pohlcuje "
"krátkovlnné infračervené svetlo, ale odráža viditeľné svetlo, zatiaľ čo "
"oblaky vo všeobecnosti odrážajú v oboch vlnových dĺžkach. Snehová pokrývka "
"je znázornená jasnou sýtomodrou farbou.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalised difference snow index (NDSI) can be used to differentiate "
"between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the short-wave infrared "
"light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is generally "
"reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in bright vivid "
"blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný snehový index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný snehový index (NDSI) sa dá použiť na rozlíšenie "
"oblačnosti od snehovej pokrývky, pretože sneh pohlcuje krátkovlnné "
"infračervené svetlo, ale odráža viditeľné svetlo, zatiaľ čo oblaky vo "
"všeobecnosti odrážajú v oboch vlnových dĺžkach. Snehová pokrývka je "
"znázornená jasnou sýtomodrou farbou.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"This script aims to display the Earth in beautiful natural color images. It "
"uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to even out the "
"exposure.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Prirodzené farby s optimalizovanými svetlými tónmi\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript sa snaží zobraziť Zem v krásnych snímkach s prirodzenými "
"farbami. Využíva optimalizáciu svetlých tónov, aby sa predišlo prepáleným "
"pixelom a vyrovnala expozícia.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 12, 8, 2 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared (SWIR) band 12 to differentiate "
"among different rock types (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Each rock "
"and mineral type reflects short-wave infrared light differently, making it "
"possible to map out geology by comparing reflected SWIR light. Near "
"infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation and band 2 detects moisture, "
"both contributing to differentiation of ground materials. The composite is "
"useful for finding geological formations and features (e.g. faults, "
"fractures), lithology (e.g. granite, basalt, etc.) and mining applications.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"
msgstr ""
"# Geologický kompozit 12, 8, 2\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit využíva krátkovlnné infračervené (SWIR) pásmo 12 na "
"rozlíšenie rôznych typov hornín (pásmo je oblasť elektromagnetického "
"spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych pásmach). Každý typ "
"horniny a minerálu odráža krátkovlnné infračervené svetlo inak, čo umožňuje "
"mapovať geológiu porovnávaním odrazeného svetla SWIR. Pásmo 8 blízkeho "
"infračerveného svetla (NIR) zvýrazňuje vegetáciu a pásmo 2 deteguje "
"vlhkosť, pričom obe prispievajú k rozlíšeniu materiálov na povrchu. "
"Kompozit je užitočný pri hľadaní geologických útvarov a prvkov (napr. "
"zlomy, trhliny), litológie (napr. granit, čadič atď.) a pri ťažobných "
"aplikáciách.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 8, 11, 12 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses both short-wave infrared (SWIR) bands 11 and 12 to "
"differentiate among different rock types (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). Each rock and mineral type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light. Near Infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation, contributing "
"to differentiation of ground materials. Vegetation in the composite appears "
"red. The composite is useful for differentiating vegetation, and land "
"especially geologic features that can be useful for mining and mineral "
"exploration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"
msgstr ""
"# Geologický kompozit 8, 11, 12\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit využíva obe krátkovlnné infračervené (SWIR) pásma 11 a 12 na "
"rozlíšenie rôznych typov hornín (pásmo je oblasť elektromagnetického "
"spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych pásmach). Každý typ "
"horniny a minerálu odráža krátkovlnné infračervené svetlo inak, čo umožňuje "
"mapovať geológiu porovnávaním odrazeného svetla SWIR. Pásmo 8 blízkeho "
"infračerveného svetla (NIR) zvýrazňuje vegetáciu a prispieva k rozlíšeniu "
"materiálov na povrchu. Vegetácia sa v kompozite javí červená. Kompozit je "
"užitočný na rozlišovanie vegetácie a krajiny, najmä geologických prvkov, "
"ktoré môžu byť užitočné pre ťažbu a prieskum nerastov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií [tu.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, visualizes wildfires using "
"Sentinel-2 data. It combines natural color background with some NIR/SWIR "
"data for smoke penetration and more detail, while adding highlights from "
"B11 and B12 to show fires in red and orange colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"
msgstr ""
"# Lesné požiare\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript, ktorý vytvoril Pierre Markuse, vizualizuje lesné požiare "
"pomocou údajov Sentinel-2. Kombinuje pozadie v prirodzených farbách s "
"niektorými údajmi NIR/SWIR na preniknutie dymom a získanie väčšieho "
"detailu, pričom pridáva zvýraznenia z B11 a B12, aby ukázal požiare v "
"červených a oranžových farbách.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, based on the Pierre Markuse wildfire script, detects and "
"visualizes wildfires using Landsat 8/9 thermal and visible bands. It "
"combines natural color (B2, B3, B4) with thermal band (B10) analysis to "
"detect temperature anomalies and create a red-orange-white glow effect "
"highlighting fire locations.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"
msgstr ""
"# Lesné požiare\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript, založený na skripte Pierra Markuse pre lesné požiare, "
"deteguje a vizualizuje lesné požiare pomocou termálnych a viditeľných "
"pásiem Landsat 8/9. Kombinuje prirodzené farby (B2, B3, B4) s analýzou "
"termálneho pásma (B10) na zistenie teplotných anomálií a vytvorenie "
"červeno-oranžovo-bieleho žiariaceho efektu zvýrazňujúceho miesta požiarov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/main/"
"landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, uses multiple bands (a band is a "
"region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth "
"in different bands) and saturation and brightness control to enhance the "
"true color visualization.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Vylepšené skutočné farby\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript, ktorý vytvoril Pierre Markuse, využíva viacero pásiem (pásmo "
"je oblasť elektromagnetického spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v "
"rôznych pásmach) a reguláciu sýtosti a jasu na vylepšenie vizualizácie v "
"skutočných farbách.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"

msgid ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index takes advantage of the wider spectrum of Visible, "
"Red-Edge, NIR and SWIR bands.\n"
"\n"
"Values description:()=> The range of values for the index is `-1` to `1` "
"for burn scars, and `1` - `6` for active fires. Different fire intensities "
"may result in different thresholds; the current values were calibrated, as "
"per original author, on mostly Mediterranen regions.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"
msgstr ""
"# Index vyhorenej plochy\n"
"\n"
"Index vyhorenej plochy využíva širšie spektrum pásiem viditeľného svetla, "
"červeného okraja (Red-Edge), NIR a SWIR.\n"
"\n"
"Opis hodnôt:()=> Rozsah hodnôt indexu je od `-1` do `1` pre jazvy po "
"požiaroch a `1` - `6` pre aktívne požiare. Rôzne intenzity požiarov môžu "
"mať za následok rôzne prahové hodnoty; súčasné hodnoty boli podľa pôvodného "
"autora kalibrované hlavne na stredomorských oblastiach.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Burn Ratio is frequently used to estimate burn severity. It uses "
"near-infrared (NIR) and shortwave-infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. Healthy "
"vegetation has a high reflectance in the near-infrared portion of the "
"spectrum, and a low short-wave infrared reflectance. On the other hand, "
"burned areas have a high shortwave infrared reflectance but low reflectance "
"in the near infrared Darker pixels indicate burned areas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný pomer vyhorenia (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný pomer vyhorenia sa často používa na odhad závažnosti "
"vyhorenia. Využíva blízke infračervené (NIR) a krátkovlnné infračervené "
"(SWIR) vlnové dĺžky. Zdravá vegetácia má vysokú odrazivosť v blízkej "
"infračervenej časti spektra a nízku odrazivosť v krátkovlnnom infračervenom "
"svetle. Na druhej strane, vyhorené oblasti majú vysokú odrazivosť v "
"krátkovlnnom infračervenom svetle, ale nízku odrazivosť v blízkom "
"infračervenom svetle. Tmavšie pixely označujú vyhorené oblasti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/nbr/)"
"."

msgid ""
"# Atmospheric penetration\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses different bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) in the non-visible part of the electromagnetic spectrum to reduce "
"the influence of the atmosphere in the image. Short wave infrared bands 11 "
"and 12 are highly reflected by the heated areas, making them useful for "
"fire and burned area mapping. Near infrared band 8, is on contrary, highly "
"reflected by vegetation, which signifies absence of fire. Vegetation "
"appears blue, displaying details related to the vegetation vigor. Healthy "
"vegetation is shown in light blue while the stressed, sparse or/and arid "
"vegetation appears in dull blue. Urban features are white, grey, cyan or "
"purple.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosférická penetrácia\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit využíva rôzne pásma (pásmo je oblasť elektromagnetického "
"spektra; satelitný senzor môže snímať Zem v rôznych pásmach) v neviditeľnej "
"časti elektromagnetického spektra na zníženie vplyvu atmosféry na snímku. "
"Krátkovlnné infračervené pásma 11 a 12 sú silno odrážané zahriatymi "
"oblasťami, vďaka čomu sú užitočné na mapovanie požiarov a vyhorených plôch. "
"Pásmo 8 blízkeho infračerveného svetla je naopak silno odrážané vegetáciou, "
"čo znamená neprítomnosť požiaru. Vegetácia sa javí modrá a zobrazuje "
"detaily súvisiace so životaschopnosťou vegetácie. Zdravá vegetácia je "
"zobrazená svetlomodrou, zatiaľ čo stresovaná, riedka alebo suchá vegetácia "
"sa javí matnomodrá. Mestské prvky sú biele, sivé, azúrové alebo fialové.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií [tu.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"

msgid ""
"# Barren Soil Visualization\n"
"\n"
"The Barren Soil Visualization can be useful for soil mapping, to "
"investigate the location of landslides or the extent of erosion in "
"non-vegetated areas. This visualization shows all vegetation in green and "
"the barren ground in red. Water appears black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) and "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizácia holej pôdy\n"
"\n"
"Vizualizácia holej pôdy môže byť užitočná pri mapovaní pôdy, pri skúmaní "
"umiestnenia zosuvov pôdy alebo rozsahu erózie v oblastiach bez vegetácie. "
"Táto vizualizácia zobrazuje všetku vegetáciu zelenou a holú zem červenou. "
"Voda sa javí čierna.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) a "
"[tu.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-satellite-"
"images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"

msgid ""
"# True Color with IR Highlights composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite enhances the true color visualization by adding the "
"shortwave infrared wavelengths to amplify details. It displays heated areas "
"in red/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit v skutočných farbách so zvýraznením IR\n"
"\n"
"Tento kompozit vylepšuje vizualizáciu v skutočných farbách pridaním "
"krátkovlnných infračervených vlnových dĺžok na zvýraznenie detailov. "
"Zahriate oblasti zobrazuje červenou/oranžovou farbou.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-9"
"d1de0133733)"

msgid ""
"# Detection of Burned Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script is used to detect large scale recently burned areas. Pixels "
"colored red highlight burned areas, and all other pixels are returned in "
"true color. The script sometimes overestimates burned areas over water and "
"clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"
msgstr ""
"# Detekcia vyhorených plôch\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript sa používa na detekciu rozsiahlych nedávno vyhorených plôch. "
"Pixely vyfarbené načerveno zvýrazňujú vyhorené plochy a všetky ostatné "
"pixely sú vrátené v skutočných farbách. Skript niekedy nadhodnocuje "
"vyhorené plochy nad vodou a oblakmi.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"

msgid ""
"# Scene classification\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scene classification was developed to distinguish between cloudy pixels, "
"clear pixels and water pixels of Sentinel-2 data and is a result of ESA's "
"Scene classification algorithm. Twelve different classifications are "
"provided including classes of clouds, vegetation, soils/desert, water and "
"snow. It does not constitute a land cover classification map in a strict "
"sense.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."
msgstr ""
"# Klasifikácia scény\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Klasifikácia scény bola vyvinutá na rozlíšenie oblačných pixelov, čistých "
"pixelov a vodných pixelov v údajoch Sentinel-2 a je výsledkom algoritmu "
"klasifikácie scény ESA. Poskytuje sa dvanásť rôznych klasifikácií vrátane "
"tried oblakov, vegetácie, pôd/púští, vody a snehu. Nepredstavuje mapu "
"klasifikácie krajinnej pokrývky v striktnom zmysle.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."

msgid ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI) is estimated based on the "
"chlorophyll content in terrestrial vegetation and can be used to monitor "
"vegetation condition and health. Low OTCI values usually signify water, "
"sand or snow. Extremely high values, displayed with white, usually suggest "
"the absence of chlorophyll as well. They generally represent either bare "
"ground, rock or clouds. The chlorophyll values in between range from red "
"(low chlorophyll values) to dark green (high chlorophyll values) can be "
"used to determine vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"
msgstr ""
"# Index pozemského chlorofylu (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Index pozemského chlorofylu (OTCI) sa odhaduje na základe obsahu chlorofylu "
"v pozemskej vegetácii a dá sa použiť na monitorovanie stavu a zdravia "
"vegetácie. Nízke hodnoty OTCI zvyčajne označujú vodu, piesok alebo sneh. "
"Extrémne vysoké hodnoty, zobrazené bielou, zvyčajne naznačujú tiež "
"neprítomnosť chlorofylu. Vo všeobecnosti predstavujú holú zem, skalu alebo "
"oblaky. Hodnoty chlorofylu medzi nimi, od červenej (nízke hodnoty "
"chlorofylu) po tmavozelenú (vysoké hodnoty chlorofylu), sa dajú použiť na "
"určenie zdravia vegetácie.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"

msgid ""
"# Topographic Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a visualisation with green colours representing lowland "
"elevations and earth colours as mountainous elevations. The script uses "
"discrete classes rather than the continuous visualisations in the other DEM "
"layers.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"
msgstr ""
"# Topografická vizualizácia\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript vracia vizualizáciu, v ktorej zelené farby predstavujú nížinné "
"nadmorské výšky a zemité farby horské nadmorské výšky. Skript používa "
"diskrétne triedy namiesto spojitých vizualizácií v ostatných vrstvách DEM.\n"
"\n"
"V evalscripte je možné nastaviť vlastné minimálne a maximálne hodnoty tak, "
"že sa defaultVis nastaví na false a premenné min a max na požadované "
"hodnoty.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"

msgid ""
"# Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a color visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Farebná vizualizácia\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript vracia farebnú vizualizáciu digitálneho modelu terénu, pričom "
"hraniciam nadmorských výšok priraďuje spojité farby.\n"
"\n"
"V evalscripte je možné nastaviť vlastné minimálne a maximálne hodnoty tak, "
"že sa defaultVis nastaví na false a premenné min a max na požadované "
"hodnoty.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Grayscale Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a grayscale visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizácia v odtieňoch sivej\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript vracia vizualizáciu digitálneho modelu terénu v odtieňoch "
"sivej, pričom hraniciam nadmorských výšok priraďuje spojité farby.\n"
"\n"
"V evalscripte je možné nastaviť vlastné minimálne a maximálne hodnoty tak, "
"že sa defaultVis nastaví na false a premenné min a max na požadované "
"hodnoty.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"

msgid ""
"# Sepia Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a sepia visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"
msgstr ""
"# Sépiová vizualizácia\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript vracia sépiovú vizualizáciu digitálneho modelu terénu, pričom "
"hraniciam nadmorských výšok priraďuje spojité farby.\n"
"\n"
"V evalscripte je možné nastaviť vlastné minimálne a maximálne hodnoty tak, "
"že sa defaultVis nastaví na false a premenné min a max na požadované "
"hodnoty.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It displays water areas in blue (partially black) and "
"land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban areas are displayed in a "
"light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas in mustard green and "
"bare ground in a darker green.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. In order not to confuse "
"cryogenic features with non-cryogenic ones, some general information about "
"the location is helpful in interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Vylepšená vizualizácia\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript kombinuje gamma0 polarizácií VV a VH do vizualizácie v "
"nepravých farbách. Vodné plochy zobrazuje modrou (čiastočne čiernou) a "
"pevninu v rôznych odtieňoch žltej/zelenej. Mestské oblasti sú zobrazené "
"svetlou zelenožltou (smerom k bielej), zarastené oblasti horčicovozelenou a "
"holá zem tmavšou zelenou.\n"
"\n"
"Pri zasnežených a zaľadnených oblastiach sa vizualizácia môže meniť od "
"svetlej zelenožltej cez jasnejšiu zelenú až po tmavohnedú alebo dokonca "
"čiernu. Aby sa kryogénne prvky nezamieňali s nekryogénnymi, je pri "
"interpretácii snímky užitočná určitá všeobecná informácia o lokalite."

msgid ""
"# SAR False Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations of "
"Sentinel-1 SAR data into a false color visualization. Water areas appear in "
"blue (partially black) and land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban "
"areas are displayed in light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas "
"in mustard green, and bare ground in darker green. The visualization "
"supports a wide range of monitoring applications, including ice and ship "
"tracking, agriculture and deforestation monitoring, and emergency response "
"scenarios such as flood and volcano observation.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. Some general knowledge of "
"the location is helpful to avoid confusing cryogenic features with other "
"land cover types.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizácia SAR v nepravých farbách\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript kombinuje gamma0 polarizácií VV a VH údajov SAR zo Sentinel-1 "
"do vizualizácie v nepravých farbách. Vodné plochy sa javia modré (čiastočne "
"čierne) a pevnina v rôznych odtieňoch žltej/zelenej. Mestské oblasti sú "
"zobrazené svetlou zelenožltou (smerom k bielej), zarastené oblasti "
"horčicovozelenou a holá zem tmavšou zelenou. Vizualizácia podporuje širokú "
"škálu monitorovacích aplikácií vrátane sledovania ľadu a lodí, "
"monitorovania poľnohospodárstva a odlesňovania a scenárov núdzovej reakcie, "
"ako je pozorovanie povodní a sopiek.\n"
"\n"
"Pri zasnežených a zaľadnených oblastiach sa vizualizácia môže meniť od "
"svetlej zelenožltej cez jasnejšiu zelenú až po tmavohnedú alebo dokonca "
"čiernu. Určitá všeobecná znalosť lokality je užitočná, aby sa kryogénne "
"prvky nezamieňali s inými typmi krajinnej pokrývky.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# Urban Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script uses Sentinel-1 SAR VH and VV polarisations to highlight urban "
"areas and buildings. Structures appear in different colours depending on "
"their backscatter characteristics: purple indicates high VH reflectance, "
"green indicates high VV reflectance, and white indicates high reflectance "
"in both. The red channel is restricted to pixels where VH exceeds 0.5, "
"helping separate buildings from bare soil. The script is useful for "
"monitoring urban expansion, assessing building density, and identifying "
"structures in flood-prone areas. Note that in mountainous terrain, steep "
"slopes and snow can produce similar signals, making it difficult to "
"separate urban areas from other features.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# Mestské oblasti\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript využíva polarizácie VH a VV SAR zo Sentinel-1 na zvýraznenie "
"mestských oblastí a budov. Štruktúry sa javia v rôznych farbách v "
"závislosti od ich charakteristík spätného rozptylu: fialová označuje vysokú "
"odrazivosť VH, zelená vysokú odrazivosť VV a biela vysokú odrazivosť v "
"oboch. Červený kanál je obmedzený na pixely, kde VH presahuje 0,5, čo "
"pomáha oddeliť budovy od holej pôdy. Skript je užitočný na monitorovanie "
"rozrastania miest, posudzovanie hustoty zástavby a identifikáciu štruktúr v "
"oblastiach ohrozených povodňami. Upozorňujeme, že v horskom teréne môžu "
"strmé svahy a sneh vytvárať podobné signály, čo sťažuje oddelenie mestských "
"oblastí od iných prvkov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# SAR Deforestation Detection\n"
"\n"
"This script processes Sentinel-1 VV and VH polarisation bands to detect "
"deforestation and forest degradation. It converts the backscatter values "
"into polar form to derive vector length and angle, which discriminate "
"between water, forest, and bare soil. Water and bare soil appear black, "
"forested areas are rendered in green gradients, and degraded or cleared "
"areas appear in red — with stronger colours indicating higher "
"classification confidence. The script is useful for monitoring forest loss "
"and land-use change over time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."
msgstr ""
"# Detekcia odlesňovania pomocou SAR\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript spracúva polarizačné pásma VV a VH zo Sentinel-1 na detekciu "
"odlesňovania a degradácie lesov. Prevádza hodnoty spätného rozptylu do "
"polárneho tvaru, aby odvodil dĺžku a uhol vektora, ktoré rozlišujú vodu, "
"les a holú pôdu. Voda a holá pôda sa javia čierne, zalesnené oblasti sú "
"vykreslené v zelených prechodoch a degradované alebo vyrúbané oblasti sa "
"javia červené — pričom sýtejšie farby naznačujú vyššiu spoľahlivosť "
"klasifikácie. Skript je užitočný na monitorovanie úbytku lesov a zmien "
"využitia územia v čase.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."

msgid ""
"# Water Surface Roughness\n"
"\n"
"This script visualizes water surface roughness using Sentinel-1 SAR data. "
"SAR backscatter is highly sensitive to the roughness of the water surface: "
"calm water reflects radar energy away from the sensor and appears dark, "
"while rough or wind-driven water scatters energy back and appears brighter. "
"Variations in surface roughness reveal oceanographic and maritime features "
"such as wind patterns, sea currents, internal waves, and ship wakes. Oil "
"spills dampen surface waves and appear as dark patches against the "
"surrounding rougher water. The visualization supports maritime monitoring "
"applications including ship tracking, oil pollution detection, and "
"observation of ocean circulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Drsnosť vodnej hladiny\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript vizualizuje drsnosť vodnej hladiny pomocou údajov SAR zo "
"Sentinel-1. Spätný rozptyl SAR je veľmi citlivý na drsnosť vodnej hladiny: "
"pokojná voda odráža radarovú energiu mimo senzora a javí sa tmavá, zatiaľ "
"čo rozvlnená alebo vetrom poháňaná voda rozptyľuje energiu späť a javí sa "
"jasnejšia. Zmeny drsnosti hladiny odhaľujú oceánografické a námorné javy, "
"ako sú vzory vetra, morské prúdy, vnútorné vlny a brázdy za loďami. Ropné "
"škvrny tlmia povrchové vlny a javia sa ako tmavé škvrny na okolitej "
"drsnejšej vode. Vizualizácia podporuje aplikácie námorného monitorovania "
"vrátane sledovania lodí, detekcie znečistenia ropou a pozorovania "
"cirkulácie oceánov.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB ratio\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It uses the VV polarization in the red channel, the VH "
"polarization in the green channel, and a ratio of VH/VV in the blue "
"channel. It shows water areas in dark red (black), urban areas in yellow, "
"vegetated areas in turquoise, and bare ground in dark purple.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light yellow to "
"blue to red. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with non-cryogenic "
"ones, some general information about the location is helpful in "
"interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Pomer RGB\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript kombinuje gamma0 polarizácií VV a VH do vizualizácie v "
"nepravých farbách. V červenom kanáli používa polarizáciu VV, v zelenom "
"kanáli polarizáciu VH a v modrom kanáli pomer VH/VV. Vodné plochy zobrazuje "
"tmavočervenou (čiernou), mestské oblasti žltou, zarastené oblasti "
"tyrkysovou a holú zem tmavofialovou.\n"
"\n"
"Pri zasnežených a zaľadnených oblastiach sa vizualizácia môže meniť od "
"svetložltej cez modrú po červenú. Aby sa kryogénne prvky nezamieňali s "
"nekryogénnymi, je pri interpretácii snímky užitočná určitá všeobecná "
"informácia o lokalite."

msgid ""
"# SAR Urban\n"
"\n"
"The script is useful for locating urban areas and individual buildings. It "
"uses the gamma0 of the VH polarization and the VV polarizations to "
"highlight different buildings and topology orientations with purple and "
"green colors. It can be used to track urban expansion, estimate building "
"type, or locate buildings in risk areas (e.g., flooding).\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from white to purple to "
"dark blue or even black. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with "
"non-cryogenic ones, some general information about the location is helpful "
"to interpret the image. \n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR pre mestské oblasti\n"
"\n"
"Skript je užitočný na lokalizáciu mestských oblastí a jednotlivých budov. "
"Využíva gamma0 polarizácie VH a polarizácie VV na zvýraznenie rôznych budov "
"a orientácií topológie fialovou a zelenou farbou. Dá sa použiť na "
"sledovanie rozrastania miest, odhad typu budov alebo lokalizáciu budov v "
"rizikových oblastiach (napr. pri povodniach).\n"
"\n"
"Pri zasnežených a zaľadnených oblastiach sa vizualizácia môže meniť od "
"bielej cez fialovú po tmavomodrú alebo dokonca čiernu. Aby sa kryogénne "
"prvky nezamieňali s nekryogénnymi, je pri interpretácii snímky užitočná "
"určitá všeobecná informácia o lokalite. \n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# HH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships. It provides good contrast between water and "
"land surfaces. Compared to the linear gamma0 visualization, the decibel "
"gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HH - decibelová gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript zobrazuje vizualizáciu gamma0 polarizácie HH v odtieňoch "
"sivej. Polarizácia HH je v porovnaní s polarizáciou VV menej citlivá na "
"drsnosť povrchu, a preto sa používa na detekciu objektov a pevných cieľov, "
"ako sú lode. Poskytuje dobrý kontrast medzi vodnými a pevninskými povrchmi. "
"V porovnaní s vizualizáciou lineárnej gamma0 zahŕňa vizualizácia "
"decibelovej gamma0 logaritmické škálovanie údajov."

msgid ""
"# HH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships."
msgstr ""
"# HH - lineárna gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript zobrazuje vizualizáciu gamma0 polarizácie HH v odtieňoch "
"sivej. Polarizácia HH je v porovnaní s polarizáciou VV menej citlivá na "
"drsnosť povrchu, a preto sa používa na detekciu objektov a pevných cieľov, "
"ako sú lode."

msgid ""
"# HV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HV - decibelová gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Tento skript zobrazuje vizualizáciu gamma0 polarizácie HV v odtieňoch "
"sivej. Hodnoty krížovej polarizácie (HV) sú vo všeobecnosti nižšie (tmavšia "
"vizualizácia) ako pri súbežnej polarizácii (HH, VV). Polarizácia HV má "
"vyššie hodnoty pre povrchy charakterizované objemovým rozptylom, napr. "
"konáre, suché pôdy alebo porasty (svetlejšia farba vo vizualizácii) a "
"nižšie pre povrchy s malým alebo žiadnym rozptylom (tmavšia farba vo "
"vizualizácii). V porovnaní s vizualizáciou lineárnej gamma0 zahŕňa "
"vizualizácia decibelovej gamma0 logaritmické škálovanie údajov."

msgid ""
"# HV - linear gamma0\n"
