msgid ""
"# Total suspended matter concentration\n"
"\n"
"Satellite-derived total suspended matter (TSM) is a measure of the "
"concentration of particulate material in surface water such as mud, silt "
"and other fine-grainded sedimentss, including organic and inorganic "
"fractions. The TSM product is calculated based on the MERIS 1999 Baseline "
"Atmospheric Correction and the OCI neural net TSM algorithm by [Hieronymi "
"et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). The product has variable accuracy and schould be "
"considert experimental.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"
msgstr ""
"# Koncentrácia celkovej suspendovanej hmoty\n"
"\n"
"Satelitne odvodená celková suspendovaná hmota (TSM) je mierou koncentrácie "
"časticového materiálu v povrchovej vode, ako je bahno, kal a iné jemnozrnné "
"sedimenty, vrátane organických a anorganických frakcií. Produkt TSM sa "
"vypočítava na základe atmosférickej korekcie MERIS 1999 Baseline a "
"neurónového algoritmu OCI pre TSM od [Hieronymi et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). Produkt má premenlivú presnosť a mal by sa "
"považovať za experimentálny.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"

msgid ""
"# Aerosol optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"Aerosol optical thickness (AOT) is a measure of the extent to which "
"aerosols in the atmosphere prevent the transmission of light through "
"absorption and scattering. Optical thickness, also knwon as optical depth "
"depends on the physical nature, the shape and the concentration of "
"particles. AOT is often used in climatology and atmospheric research to "
"assess the effects of aerosols on weather, climate, and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Optická hrúbka aerosólov\n"
"\n"
"Optická hrúbka aerosólov (AOT) je mierou toho, do akej miery aerosóly v "
"atmosfére bránia prenosu svetla absorpciou a rozptylom. Optická hrúbka, "
"známa aj ako optická hĺbka, závisí od fyzikálnej povahy, tvaru a "
"koncentrácie častíc. AOT sa často používa v klimatológii a atmosférickom "
"výskume na posúdenie vplyvu aerosólov na počasie, klímu a kvalitu ovzdušia.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Photosynthetically active radiation\n"
"\n"
"The Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) visualization displays the "
"instantaneous PAR at the water surface. It was adopted from FERIS and "
"developed based on an algorithm by [Aiken and Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). The PAR is a "
"measure of the energy flux from the sun in the wavelenght range of 400–700 "
"nm. It is often used to convert measured chlorophyll concentration into an "
"estimate of ocen productivity and from this an estimate of the carbon "
"sequestration. As such, it plays an important role in modelling of the "
"carbon-cycle.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Fotosynteticky aktívne žiarenie\n"
"\n"
"Vizualizácia fotosynteticky aktívneho žiarenia (PAR) zobrazuje okamžité PAR "
"na hladine vody. Bola prevzatá z FERIS a vyvinutá na základe algoritmu od "
"[Aiken a Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). PAR je "
"mierou toku energie zo Slnka vo vlnovom rozsahu 400–700 nm. Často sa "
"používa na prepočet nameranej koncentrácie chlorofylu na odhad produktivity "
"oceánu a z nej na odhad ukladania uhlíka. Ako také zohráva dôležitú úlohu "
"pri modelovaní uhlíkového cyklu.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Diffuse attenuation coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The diffuse attenuation coefficient at 490 nm is a measure of how the "
"intensity of light decreases as it passes through a column of water. It "
"quantifies the rate at which light is absorbed and scattered by water and "
"its constituents, such as phytoplankton, dissolved organic matter and "
"suspended particles. This coefficient is crucial for understanding "
"underwater light environments and is widely used in marine biology, "
"oceanography and environmental science. It's calculated as described in "
"[Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Koeficient difúzneho útlmu\n"
"\n"
"Koeficient difúzneho útlmu pri 490 nm je mierou toho, ako klesá intenzita "
"svetla pri prechode vodným stĺpcom. Vyjadruje rýchlosť, akou je svetlo "
"pohlcované a rozptyľované vodou a jej zložkami, ako sú fytoplanktón, "
"rozpustená organická látka a suspendované častice. Tento koeficient je "
"kľúčový pre pochopenie podvodného svetelného prostredia a je široko "
"využívaný v morskej biológii, oceánografii a environmentálnej vede. "
"Vypočítava sa podľa postupu opísaného v [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product shows an "
"overestimation in the transition zones between glint and off-glint and has "
"a systematic overestimation of about 20%.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Integrovaný stĺpec vodnej pary\n"
"\n"
"Integrovaný stĺpec vodnej pary zobrazuje vodnú paru integrovanú cez "
"atmosférický stĺpec. Zobrazuje sa v kg/m2 a vypočítava sa na základe pásma "
"18 (885 nm) a pásma 19 (900 nm). Produkt vykazuje nadhodnotenie v "
"prechodových zónach medzi slnečným odleskom a oblasťou bez odleskov a má "
"systematické nadhodnotenie približne 20 %.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (open waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Koncentrácia riasových pigmentov (otvorené vody)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) vyvinutý [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) a CI vyvinutý [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (complex waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Koncentrácia riasových pigmentov (zložité vody)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) vyvinutý [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) a CI vyvinutý [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# CDM absorption coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The Coloured Detrital and Dissolved Material (CDM) absorption coefficient "
"at 443 nm indicates the fraction of incident light that is absorbed by both "
"detrital particles and colored dissolved organic matter (CDOM). Dissolved "
"organic matter is an important component of the oceanic carbon cycle. It is "
"also used as an indicator for assessing the impact of terrigenous inputs in "
"coastal waters.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78e3"
"b673b)."
msgstr ""
"# Absorpčný koeficient CDM\n"
"\n"
"Absorpčný koeficient farebnej detritovej a rozpustenej hmoty (CDM) pri 443 "
"nm udáva podiel dopadajúceho svetla, ktorý je pohlcovaný detritovými "
"časticami aj farebnou rozpustenou organickou látkou (CDOM). Rozpustená "
"organická látka je dôležitou súčasťou oceánskeho uhlíkového cyklu. Používa "
"sa aj ako ukazovateľ na posúdenie vplyvu pozemských vstupov v pobrežných "
"vodách.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78e3b6"
"73b)."

msgid ""
"# Aerosol Angstrom exponent\n"
"\n"
"The Aerosol Angstrom exponent is a parameter that describes how the optical "
"thickness of aerosols in the atmosphere varies with wavelength. It provides "
"information about the size distribution of aerosol particles, with higher "
"values indicating smaller particles and lower values indicating larger "
"particles. This exponent is often used in atmospheric research and "
"climatology to analyse the properties of aerosols and their effects on "
"climate and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Angströmov exponent aerosólov\n"
"\n"
"Angströmov exponent aerosólov je parameter, ktorý opisuje, ako sa optická "
"hrúbka aerosólov v atmosfére mení s vlnovou dĺžkou. Poskytuje informácie o "
"veľkostnom rozdelení aerosólových častíc, pričom vyššie hodnoty znamenajú "
"menšie častice a nižšie hodnoty väčšie častice. Tento exponent sa často "
"používa v atmosférickom výskume a klimatológii na analýzu vlastností "
"aerosólov a ich vplyvov na klímu a kvalitu ovzdušia.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 779\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 779 is based on the NIR band (band "
"17) with a wavelength of 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Rektifikovaná odrazivosť 779\n"
"\n"
"Produkt rektifikovanej odrazivosti je vedľajším produktom produktu GIFAPAR. "
"Zobrazuje virtuálnu odrazivosť, ktorá je do veľkej miery bez atmosférických "
"a uhlových vplyvov a je dobrým priblížením odrazivosti vrchnej časti "
"porastu. Rektifikovaná odrazivosť 779 je založená na pásme NIR (pásmo 17) s "
"vlnovou dĺžkou 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 681\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 681 is based on the red band (band "
"10) with a wavelength of 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Rektifikovaná odrazivosť 681\n"
"\n"
"Produkt rektifikovanej odrazivosti je vedľajším produktom produktu GIFAPAR. "
"Zobrazuje virtuálnu odrazivosť, ktorá je do veľkej miery bez atmosférických "
"a uhlových vplyvov a je dobrým priblížením odrazivosti vrchnej časti "
"porastu. Rektifikovaná odrazivosť 681 je založená na červenom pásme (pásmo "
"10) s vlnovou dĺžkou 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"The Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR) is a bio-geophysical product used to study the "
"photosynthetic process of plants and is often used in diagnostic and "
"predictive models computing primary productivity of the vegetation "
"canopies. In addition, this parameter is also an input for the estimation "
"of assimilation of CO2 in vegetation. GIFAPAR ranges from 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."
msgstr ""
"# Zelený okamžitý podiel absorbovaného fotosynteticky využiteľného žiarenia "
"(GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"Zelený okamžitý podiel absorbovaného fotosynteticky využiteľného žiarenia "
"(GIFAPAR) je biogeofyzikálny produkt používaný na štúdium fotosyntetického "
"procesu rastlín a často sa využíva v diagnostických a prediktívnych "
"modeloch počítajúcich primárnu produktivitu vegetačných porastov. Tento "
"parameter je navyše vstupom pre odhad asimilácie CO2 vo vegetácii. GIFAPAR "
"sa pohybuje v rozsahu 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product provides stable "
"and high quality results, but shows a systematic overestimation of about "
"9%–13% copared to ground base reference.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Integrovaný stĺpec vodnej pary\n"
"\n"
"Integrovaný stĺpec vodnej pary zobrazuje vodnú paru integrovanú cez "
"atmosférický stĺpec. Zobrazuje sa v kg/m2 a vypočítava sa na základe pásma "
"18 (885 nm) a pásma 19 (900 nm). Produkt poskytuje stabilné a kvalitné "
"výsledky, ale vykazuje systematické nadhodnotenie približne 9 %–13 % v "
"porovnaní s pozemnou referenciou.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Land Surface Temperature (LST)\n"
"\n"
"The Land Surface Temperature (LST) product provides the temperature of the "
"Earth's surface as retrieved from the SLSTR thermal infrared channels. LST "
"is a key parameter in the physics of land surface, controlling the "
"partitioning of energy between the atmosphere and the land surface. It is "
"used in climate change monitoring, drought monitoring, and urban heat "
"island studies.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-Products-"
"L2-LST-Products)."
msgstr ""
"# Teplota zemského povrchu (LST)\n"
"\n"
"Produkt teploty zemského povrchu (LST) poskytuje teplotu povrchu Zeme "
"získanú z termálnych infračervených kanálov SLSTR. LST je kľúčový parameter "
"vo fyzike zemského povrchu, ktorý riadi rozdelenie energie medzi atmosférou "
"a zemským povrchom. Používa sa pri monitorovaní zmeny klímy, monitorovaní "
"sucha a štúdiách mestských tepelných ostrovov.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-Products-L2"
"-LST-Products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) is a dimensionless index "
"that describes the difference between visible and near-infrared reflectance "
"of vegetation cover. It can be used to estimate the density of vegetation "
"cover and monitor vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index (NDVI) je bezrozmerný index, ktorý "
"opisuje rozdiel medzi odrazivosťou vegetačného krytu vo viditeľnom a "
"blízkom infračervenom svetle. Dá sa použiť na odhad hustoty vegetačného "
"krytu a monitorovanie zdravia vegetácie.\n"
"\n"
"Viac informácií "
"[tu](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index is a spectral index indicating "
"the greenness of the vegetation."
msgstr ""
"Normalizovaný diferenčný vegetačný index je spektrálny index udávajúci "
"zeleň vegetácie."

msgid ""
"Number of clear-sky surface reflectance used for the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Počet odrazivostí povrchu za jasnej oblohy použitých na inverziu "
"bidirekčnej distribučnej funkcie odrazivosti."

msgid ""
"Uncertainty of the NDVI is calculated by propagating the uncertainties "
"associated to the model parameters resulting from the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Neistota NDVI sa vypočítava šírením neistôt spojených s parametrami modelu, "
"ktoré vyplývajú z inverzie bidirekčnej distribučnej funkcie odrazivosti."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given day."
msgstr "Vrstva Jazva po požiari označuje zistené jazvy po požiaroch za daný deň."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given month."
msgstr "Vrstva Jazva po požiari označuje zistené jazvy po požiaroch za daný mesiac."

msgid "Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the day of the burn detection."
msgstr "Podiel plochy pixela zasiahnutý požiarom v deň detekcie vyhorenia."

msgid ""
"Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the month of the burn "
"detection."
msgstr "Podiel plochy pixela zasiahnutý požiarom v mesiaci detekcie vyhorenia."

msgid "Probability that the burn detection corresponds to an actual burn."
msgstr "Pravdepodobnosť, že detekcia vyhorenia zodpovedá skutočnému vyhoreniu."

msgid "Day of burn in year (1-366), no burn (0) or flag (<0)."
msgstr "Deň vyhorenia v roku (1-366), žiadne vyhorenie (0) alebo príznak (<0)."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1."
msgstr "Pravdepodobnosť, že podiel vyhorenej plochy je nad 0,1."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1˝."
msgstr "Pravdepodobnosť, že podiel vyhorenej plochy je nad 0,1˝."

msgid ""
"DMP, or Dry Matter Productivity, represents the overall growth rate or dry "
"biomass increase of the vegetation, expressed in kilograms of dry matter "
"per hectare per day (kgDM/ha/day). DMP is directly related to NPP (Net "
"Primary Productivity, in gC/m²/day), but its units are customized for "
"agro-statistical purposes. "
msgstr ""
"DMP, alebo produktivita suchej hmoty (Dry Matter Productivity), predstavuje "
"celkovú rýchlosť rastu alebo prírastok suchej biomasy vegetácie vyjadrený v "
"kilogramoch suchej hmoty na hektár za deň (kgDM/ha/deň). DMP priamo súvisí "
"s NPP (čistá primárna produkcia, v gC/m²/deň), ale jeho jednotky sú "
"prispôsobené agrostatistickým účelom. "

msgid ""
"FAPAR corresponds to the fraction of photosynthetically active radiation "
"absorbed by the green elements of the canopy. The FAPAR value results "
"directly from the radiative transfer model in the canopy which is computed "
"instantaneously. It depends on canopy structure, vegetation element optical "
"properties and illumination conditions. FAPAR is very useful as input to a "
"number of primary productivity models based on simple efficiency "
"considerations."
msgstr ""
"FAPAR zodpovedá podielu fotosynteticky aktívneho žiarenia absorbovaného "
"zelenými prvkami porastu. Hodnota FAPAR vyplýva priamo z modelu radiačného "
"prenosu v poraste, ktorý sa počíta okamžite. Závisí od štruktúry porastu, "
"optických vlastností prvkov vegetácie a podmienok osvetlenia. FAPAR je "
"veľmi užitočný ako vstup do viacerých modelov primárnej produktivity "
"založených na jednoduchých úvahách o účinnosti."

msgid ""
"FCover is defined as the fraction of ground surface covered by green "
"vegetation as seen from the nadir direction. It is used to separate "
"vegetation and soil in energy balance processes, including temperature and "
"evapotranspiration. It is computed from the leaf area index and other "
"canopy structural variables and does not depend on variables such as the "
"geometry of illumination as compared to FAPAR. For this reason, it is a "
"very good candidate for the replacement of classical vegetation indices for "
"the monitoring of green vegetation. Because of the linear relationship with "
"radiometric signal, FCover will be only marginally scale dependent. Note "
"that similarly to LAI and FAPAR, only the green elements will be "
"considered, either belonging both to the overstory and understory."
msgstr ""
"FCover je definovaný ako podiel povrchu zeme pokrytý zelenou vegetáciou pri "
"pohľade z nadiru. Používa sa na oddelenie vegetácie a pôdy v procesoch "
"energetickej bilancie vrátane teploty a evapotranspirácie. Počíta sa z "
"indexu listovej plochy a ďalších štruktúrnych premenných porastu a na "
"rozdiel od FAPAR nezávisí od premenných, ako je geometria osvetlenia. Z "
"tohto dôvodu je veľmi dobrým kandidátom na nahradenie klasických "
"vegetačných indexov pri monitorovaní zelenej vegetácie. Vďaka lineárnemu "
"vzťahu s rádiometrickým signálom bude FCover závisieť od mierky iba "
"okrajovo. Upozorňujeme, že podobne ako pri LAI a FAPAR sa berú do úvahy iba "
"zelené prvky, patriace do hornej aj dolnej vrstvy porastu."

msgid ""
"Gross Primary Production (GPP) expresses a component of Primary Production "
"of ecosystems related to the creation of new organic matter by vegetation. "
"GPP is the total amount of dry matter (carbon) \"fixed\" by land plants per "
"unit time through photosynthesis (atmospheric CO2 into organic compounds). "
"A substantial fraction of GPP supports plant autotrophic respiration (Ra). "
"GPP is typically expressed as gram of carbon per square meter per day "
"(gC/m2 /day)."
msgstr ""
"Hrubá primárna produkcia (GPP) vyjadruje zložku primárnej produkcie "
"ekosystémov súvisiacu s tvorbou novej organickej hmoty vegetáciou. GPP je "
"celkové množstvo suchej hmoty (uhlíka) „fixované“ suchozemskými rastlinami "
"za jednotku času fotosyntézou (atmosférický CO2 na organické zlúčeniny). "
"Značná časť GPP slúži na autotrofné dýchanie rastlín (Ra). GPP sa zvyčajne "
"vyjadruje v gramoch uhlíka na meter štvorcový za deň (gC/m2/deň)."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
"the size of the interface for exchange of energy (including radiation) and "
"mass between the canopy and the atmosphere. This is an intrinsic canopy "
"primary variable that should not depend on observation conditions. LAI is "
"strongly non-linearly related to reflectance. Therefore, its estimation "
"from remote sensing observations is scale dependent."
msgstr ""
"LAI je definovaný ako polovica rozvinutej plochy fotosynteticky aktívnych "
"prvkov vegetácie na jednotku vodorovnej plochy zeme. Určuje veľkosť "
"rozhrania pre výmenu energie (vrátane žiarenia) a hmoty medzi porastom a "
"atmosférou. Ide o vnútornú primárnu premennú porastu, ktorá by nemala "
"závisieť od podmienok pozorovania. LAI je s odrazivosťou silne nelineárne "
"prepojený. Preto je jeho odhad z pozorovaní diaľkového prieskumu závislý od "
"mierky."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
"the size of the interface for exchange of energy (including radiation) and "
"mass between the canopy and the atmosphere. This is an intrinsic canopy "
"primary variable that should not depend on observation conditions. LAI is "
"strongly non-linearly related to reflectance."
msgstr ""
"LAI je definovaný ako polovica rozvinutej plochy fotosynteticky aktívnych "
"prvkov vegetácie na jednotku vodorovnej plochy zeme. Určuje veľkosť "
"rozhrania pre výmenu energie (vrátane žiarenia) a hmoty medzi porastom a "
"atmosférou. Ide o vnútornú primárnu premennú porastu, ktorá by nemala "
"závisieť od podmienok pozorovania. LAI je s odrazivosťou silne nelineárne "
"prepojený."

msgid ""
"\"NPP, or Net Primary Production, is an indicator of the rate at which "
"plants produce net useful chemical energy expressed in mass of carbon per "
"unit area per day (gC/m²/day).\""
msgstr ""
"„NPP, alebo čistá primárna produkcia, je ukazovateľ rýchlosti, ktorou "
"rastliny produkujú čistú využiteľnú chemickú energiu vyjadrenú v hmotnosti "
"uhlíka na jednotku plochy za deň (gC/m²/deň).“"

msgid ""
"SWI computed with a characteristic time length of 1 day. The Soil Water "
"index (SWI) provides global daily information about moisture conditions in "
"different soil depths. Near Real Time Data uses the EUMETSAT ASCAT-25km SSM "
"product in orbit format as input data. The Archive of ASCAT SWI uses "
"reprocessed SSM data from TU Wien."
msgstr ""
"SWI vypočítaný s charakteristickou časovou dĺžkou 1 deň. Index vlhkosti "
"pôdy (SWI) poskytuje globálne denné informácie o vlhkostných podmienkach v "
"rôznych hĺbkach pôdy. Údaje takmer v reálnom čase používajú ako vstup "
"produkt EUMETSAT ASCAT-25km SSM vo formáte po dráhach. Archív ASCAT SWI "
"používa opätovne spracované údaje SSM z TU Wien."

